name:Oratio at the end of the procession: Orémus. Omnípotens sempitérne Deus, qui humáno géneri;
office-part:Oratio;
occasion:Dominica in Ramis Palmarum (Missale O.P. 1939, p. 141 (Proc. p. 33));
book:set to the Dominican tone of the Orations at the Hours, Processionarium O.P. (1913), pp. 407-408 (pdf = printed + 16); text from the Missale O.P. (1939), p. 141 (Proc. p. 33);
commentary:Proc. p. 33 (Missale p. 141): "Deinde Prior absque Dóminus vobíscum, præmisso Orémus, dicat Orationem eo modo quo dicitur ad Horas", Proc. p. 33 prints it pointed: "Orémus ‡ ... fecísti ‡ concéde propítius : ut ... documénta ‡ et Resurrectiónis consórtia mereámur : Per eúmdem Christum Dóminum nostrum ‡ ℟. Amen.";
transcriber:generated by tools/hw39/gen_quad6.js with OPMassTones (js/mtones.js), Holy Week task W-B2, 2026-11-27;
